, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.  Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to erect", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to build", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  It was more difficult  in ancient times to erect such edifices than it was as time passed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you need to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bucket list ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a list of experiences someone wants to have before they die", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Now that a more modern version of the seven ancient sights is being put together, I will have to start a new bucket list.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "edifice", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a building or structure", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It was more difficult  in ancient times to erect such edifices than it was as time passed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to pave ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to cover a surface with something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It was once said that the streets were paved with gold. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "slab", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a thick piece of a material", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The houses have been built well with closely-fitting flat stone slabs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "modifications", "type": "name"}, {"content": "changes, adaptations or adjustments", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is the only ancient town where the whole topographic structure is known precisely as it was, with no later modifications or additions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adverbial Clauses: Reduced and Unreduced", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Using <span class=\"strong\">adverbial clauses</span> makes your speech and writing sound more dynamic and sophisticated.</br> When you want to express your ideas in a more concise way, you can shorten an <span class=\"strong\">adverbial clause </span>to an adverbial phrase.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you want to describe how something happens or is done, you can use <span class=\"strong\">adverbial clauses </span>of <span class=\"underline\">manner</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: </br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Being adventurous</span>, I wandered miles and miles.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">adverbial clauses</span> of <span class=\"underline\">time</span> to show when something happens. </br></br>Example:</br><span class=\"italic\"> I wandered miles and miles along it <span class=\"strong\">after leaving the tour in the morning. </span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbial clauses</span> of comparison of <span class=\"underline\">degree</span> answer the questions <span class=\"italic\">how much</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> how little</span> or <span class=\"italic\">how many? </span>  </br></br> Example:</br><span class=\"italic\">I have never been more elated and more tired than<span class=\"strong\"> at that moment.</span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart that outlines what conjunctions go with each clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adverbial Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Conjunctions/Adverb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Manner\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">as</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Time\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">before, after, as, when, while, until, as soon as, since, no sooner than,  as long as</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Degree\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">than, as</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Before you reduce an adverb clause into an adverbial phrase, make sure that the adverbial clause (subordinate clause) and the main clause have the same subject.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <span class=\"italic\">I always take a shower <span class=\"strong\">before I go to bed</span>. </br><span class=\"strong\">Before going to bed</span>, I always take a shower.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Starting in the 7th century, the walls have been and rebuilt until fairly recently. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They made as large an edifice as anywhere on Earth!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Today, you can enjoy the view while winding through the stunning countryside. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Was this not more breathtaking than any historic site I had been to?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Despite wanting to continue on, I returned to my hotel to soak my aching legs.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect vs. Simple Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense and the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> tense to refer to past events.  </br>The<span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect </span>tense refers to actions that happened in the past and have some connection to the present.  </br>The<span class=\"strong\"> Simple Past </span><span class=\"underline\">passive</span> focuses on the person or things which received a completed past action.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense refers to events that happened very recently. In these cases, you use words like <span class=\"italic\">just</span>, <span class=\"italic\">only just</span> and <span class=\"italic\">recently</span>. </br><span class=\"italic\">  I  <span class=\"strong\">have only just  returned</span> from a tour there.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect</span> in questions to ask about past experience or unusual events:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">  <span class=\"strong\">Have </span> you ever <span class=\"strong\"> been </span> to the Great Wall of China?<br>(Notice the use of the word <span class=\"italic\">ever</span> in questions.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You also use words such as <span class=\"italic\">yet </span>, <span class=\"italic\">up to now</span>, <span class=\"italic\">so far</span> and <span class=\"italic\">until now</span> when you use the<span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect</span> , since these words and phrases refer to a period of time covering the past to the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\"> How many  <span class=\"strong\">have considered  </span>trying to walk the 6,000 mile wall <span class=\"strong\">up to now</span>?<br><span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">Have</span> you <span class=\"strong\"> packed </span>your bag <span class=\"strong\">yet</span>?</br> (You use <span class=\"italic\">yet</span> in negative statements and in questions).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> <span class=\"underline\">Passive</span> reports about events.</br> You use the passive form of the Simple Past when the action is not done <span class=\"italic\">by</span> the subject but rather <span class=\"italic\">to</span> the subject. Often, it is not known who has done the action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">I'm sure they <span class=\"strong\">were not moved </span>easily. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> <span class=\"underline\">Passive</span> is:</br>  subject + <span class=\"italic\">was/were</span> + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It has just been voted one of the new wonders of the word. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Starting in the 7th century, the walls have been and rebuilt until fairly recently. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "So far, in modern times, people have only made it a few miles.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm sure they were not moved easily. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Over the years, watch towers and troop barracks were erected and other modifications were done.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The path along the wall was constructed to be like a stone paved road.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Perhaps this was accomplished by sturdier Chinese soldiers of yore.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I find out facts about the Great Wall of China.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For each fact I use sentences in the Present Perfect tense. Then add a reduced adverbial clause. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my sentences with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We discuss the correctness of the grammar structures.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online or to the library to find out facts about the Great Wall of China.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down the facts.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For each fact, use sentences in the Present Perfect tense. Then add a reduced adverbial clause. (<span class=\"italic\">Going to the Great Wall of China is something I have always wanted to do. Work on the wall started in the 7th century.</span>)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice reading your sentences aloud so they come out naturally.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read them to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the sentences together and check for grammatical errors. ", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}